WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.028
Idea. Think of a concert hall with two hundred seats. However many people queue, and however much they offer, only two hundred get in. The number is fixed.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:17.220
Before any quota, demand and supply cross at the equilibrium price, P e, and quantity, Q e.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:31.707
A quota is a legal limit on the quantity of a good that can be imported. Whatever the price, no more can be supplied. So supply becomes a vertical line at the quota. This is perfectly inelastic supply.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:43.277
Method. Step one. Find where the quota lies. A new quota below Q e, or a tighter one, goes to the left. A bigger quota moves the line right.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:56.779
Step two. Draw the vertical line and label it S one, quota. Step three. Where it meets D, draw a dashed line across to P one. Step four. Label its foot on the quantity axis Q one.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:14.005
Worked example. Here is a real question from June 2024. China introduced a quota on imports of crude oil. Draw the effect on the equilibrium price and quantity, and label the new curve, price and quantity. Three marks.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:21.941
The quota limits oil imports to less than the amount bought before. So the vertical line goes to the left of Q e.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:42.162
Draw the vertical line and label it S one, quota. It meets D above P e. Draw across to P one, higher than P e. Its foot is Q one, lower than Q e. The price of crude oil rises and less is bought. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:53.198
Common mistake. A common mistake is drawing a parallel shift of the sloping supply curve. A quota fixes quantity, so the line must be vertical.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:02:02.142
Another is putting the line on the wrong side when a quota is increased. More is allowed in, so the line moves right and the price falls.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:17.777
Your turn. Now you try. Country K sets a quota on imported sugar, below the quantity currently bought. Show the effect on the sugar market, and label the new curve, price and quantity. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:26.407
Answer. The quota is below Q e, so draw a vertical line to the left of Q e and label it S one, quota.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:37.405
Where the line meets D, read across to P one, above P e. Q one is at its foot, left of Q e. The price of sugar rises, and the quantity falls.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:48.144
Remember: find the side, draw a vertical line and label it, then mark P one where it meets D and Q one at its foot. Now try the practice questions.
